Z||000000||SLYGUY||12-03-2001||12:37 PM||||My GT is having a detonation issue.When I accelerate using 1/2 - W.O.T it will start to ping at about 3200rpm and quit abruptly at 4200 rpm with a noticeable power increase at 4200. I've ran a search and other members recommend adjusting timing. Something about the timing being too far advanced. I thought the ECM could adjust that constantly for every driving condition. Right?<P>Thank you in advance for your input.<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||12-03-2001||12:53 PM||||I think that the ECM can only adjust engine timing to a certain extent.  Unlike the DIS 4 cylinder engines, the V6's don't have 100% ECM timing control.  I believe your iming should be 8 degrees BTC, but check your label on the underside of your decklid to be sure.<P>When you set the timing, make sure you short out the terminals on your ALDL, like how you would when you want to read codes.  While it is in diagnostic mode, then check and re-set your timing. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||12-03-2001||12:59 PM||||Thank you very much.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I'll do that.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000003||K2m4||12-04-2001||07:13 PM||||did you put cheap gas in there also..i know when i use cheap gas my car has a real bad lopw octane ping ...ive gone as far as syphoning the gas tank putting the high octane stuff in and running that...just a thought<P>Kerm <BR>86 GT<BR>86 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000004||ToddAsh||12-04-2001||10:49 PM||||Can someone explain about shorting out the terminals and setting timing.Have to set mine and I didn't know about this. Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000005||camon||12-05-2001||01:41 AM||||Start the car and warm it up. <BR>Remove black cig lighter cover (2 torx screws). Using a paper clip ground pin A and B (they should be the 2 lower pins in the block towards passenger seat of car). Now start the car again (you should see the check engine light come on).<P>Now you can set the timming. As far as the correct degree of timming this is dependant upon if you have the 2.5 or the 2.8! Read your front compartment sticker it will give you the timming degree setting. If it isn't there just post what size engine you have and someone can give you the setting! If I remember correctly the 2.8 is 10 degree's, Not sure about the 2.5!<P>------------------<BR>   Keith<BR>1987 Fiero GT<p>[This message has been edited by camon (edited 12-05-2001).]||||reg||1
